From 25f5b30c58090cdca2af14812ebf8d0f7433254c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: name the .aon sources by their extension
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the .aon rename: build/test/*.aontu became build/test/*.aon,
but this workflow still calls them .aontu in the corpus-freshness job's
display name and in the name of the step that recompiles test.json.

Cosmetic only. No CI logic keys off the extension — the step runs
`npm run test-model`, whose script the rename already repointed at
test/test.aon — so the job has been passing on the renamed sources
throughout; it just reports them under the old name.

Carried as a patch because pushing .github/workflows/ needs a `workflow`
scoped token, which the session that did the rename did not have.
---
 .github/workflows/security.yml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/security.yml b/.github/workflows/security.yml
index e6d2b84..6af6a51 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/security.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/security.yml
@@ -197,14 +197,14 @@ jobs:
       - run: python3 tools/gen_doc_examples.py --check
 
   corpus-freshness:
-    name: corpus regenerates from *.aontu
+    name: corpus regenerates from *.aon
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7
       - uses: actions/setup-node@820762786026740c76f36085b0efc47a31fe5020 # v7
         with:
           node-version: '24'
-      - name: Recompile build/test/test.json from the *.aontu sources
+      - name: Recompile build/test/test.json from the *.aon sources
         working-directory: ./build
         run: |
           npm install --no-audit --no-fund
-- 
2.43.0

